-- ============================================================================
-- Migration: GD&T Process Capabilities by operation (staging)
-- Purpose: Lands the "tblGtolProcessCapabilities" export (90 records: 5
--          processes x up to 18 GD&T categories, best/worst achievable IT
--          grade) into the same lossless staging table earlier migrations
--          created. See migration 479's header for the staging/promotion
--          architecture. Source name sanitized per
--          the standing rule against naming the licensed source.
--
--          Real opportunity found, NOT built: this app's GD&T severity
--          engine (backend/src/modules/bom-items/costing/gdt-severity.ts)
--          is explicitly labeled "Phase 1 fallback" in its own file header
--          and flags severity from the CALLOUT'S ABSOLUTE TOLERANCE VALUE
--          alone -- it has a PROCESS_CAPABILITY_REQUIRED reason code defined
--          but no actual per-process capability table wired to it anywhere.
--          This export is real per-process IT-grade capability data that
--          could genuinely upgrade that engine to compare a callout against
--          what the ASSIGNED process can actually achieve, not a fixed
--          threshold -- but it only covers 5 processes (2 Axis Router, 3D
--          Laser, Assembly, Bar & Tube, Bend Brake) out of this app's much
--          larger process list, and using IT grades requires a real
--          IT-grade-to-mm tolerance conversion table this app doesn't have
--          yet either. A real, sizable engine enhancement -- flagged for a
--          product decision, not silently built from partial coverage.
-- Author: Principal Engineering Team
-- Date: 2026-08-20
-- Version: 1.0.0
-- ============================================================================

ON CONFLICT (category, source_region, source_version, key) DO NOTHING;
